# JCodeBuddy tool output. A `.jcodebuddy/` directory appears only in modules that apply
# `project-automation`, and each one carries its own .gitignore as the authority (see
# hipster-entity-example/.jcodebuddy/README.md and
# doc-hipster-entity/architecture/decisions/DEC-026.md). These entries are the
# belt-and-braces net for the root and for any module that forgets its own; the tracked
# subtrees (context/, reports/) are deliberately absent, so they stay visible in
# `git status`.
.jcodebuddy/metadata/
.jcodebuddy/agent-state/
.jcodebuddy/worktrees/

# Compatibility: the watch agent's cache/audit root before it moved under .jcodebuddy.
.watch

# Node / Gradle trees inside the tooling subprojects
vscode-jwa/node_modules
intellij-jwa/.gradle
vscode-jswa/node_modules
jswa-core/node_modules
intellij-jswa/.gradle
node_modules
.vscode-test
/webview-vscode/out
/webview-vscode/*.vsix

# The VS Code host moved under webview/, so its build output is ignored at the new path too. The two
# entries above are kept because a checkout that predates the move still has them.
webview/webview-vscode/out
webview/webview-vscode/*.vsix
# The JetBrains host's Gradle build, which was never listed because the module used to publish its own
# .gitignore.
webview/webview-jetbrains/build
webview/webview-jetbrains/.gradle
webview/webview-jetbrains/.kotlin
# The IntelliJ compiler writes `.class` files to bin/ rather than build/, so the Gradle paths above miss
# it; observed untracked on 2026-09-25 after the plugin was opened in the IDE.
webview/webview-jetbrains/bin

# Zed compiles a dev extension in place and drops the artifact next to the manifest, so this appears the
# moment someone runs `Install Dev Extension` on webview/zed/webview-zed-dev-extension. Cargo's own
# target/ is covered by the root `target/` rule above.
webview/zed/*/extension.wasm

# The standalone host publishes its port and token path inside the project it serves. Derived and
# per-machine, so it is ignored - but only this subtree: a module's `.jcodebuddy/context` and
# `.jcodebuddy/reports` are contracts and stay visible (DEC-026).
.jcodebuddy/webview

# Agent harness state. `.kilo/plans` holds untracked per-round plans; the tool's own
# config (package.json, node_modules) is covered above.
.kilo/plans
.mvn-local-repo

# Agent scratch. Deliberately NOT under `target/`: the recorded gate runs `mvn clean` on every
# invocation, so a scratch script written under target/ is deleted by the very command that
# verifies the work it enabled. `.tmp/` survives that, and being ignored it also cannot be
# swallowed by a `git add -A`. It is durable against `clean`, not against a clone: nothing here
# is ever committed or required. The rule is in AGENTS.md § 2.
.tmp/

# fs-meta's per-checkout state: the trio a watcher maintains (fs-meta/FORMAT.md) is derived output for
# whichever folder it describes, exactly like `.jcodebuddy/`'s derived subtrees, and a clone carries none
# of it. A project that wants to *commit* a trio opts it back in with a `!` rule.
.fs-meta/

# The Zig build's own output and caches, wherever a Zig port lives (fs-meta/zig when it lands, and any future
# one). The check runners pin the caches under the module so a sandboxed or CI run writes nothing outside the
# tree, and a check that compiles Java for itself writes `.java-check/` for the same reason.
zig-out/
.zig-cache/
.java-check/

# The jsx6 checkout that AGENTS.md § 2 requires for any UI work: a local clone, updated on demand
# (`git -C .jsx6 pull --ff-only`), never pinned and never committed. It sits beside `.tmp/` for the
# same reason the scratch rule gives — the recorded gate runs `clean`, so it must not live under
# target/, and it must be ignored or a `git add -A` would swallow the whole checkout.
.jsx6/

# proto/ is the driver-project area: real projects that exercise JCodeBuddy while it is under
# development. They are *not* part of this repository - each one is a repository of its own.
#
# The whole directory is ignored, with no exceptions. That is deliberate for this phase: driver
# projects are a local workspace, not something another developer checks out from here, so nothing
# under proto/ - a project's sources, its .jcodebuddy/, its .git/, its build output, or the README
# and AGENTS.md that sit in the area itself - needs to survive a clone of this repository.
proto/
node_modules/
/zig-pkg
